    "problem_statement": "Variable interpolation broken - swapped name and default values\n\nDescription\n\nVariable interpolation is not working correctly when using `${variable}` or `${variable:-default}` syntax. The variable names and default values appear to be swapped, causing incorrect substitution behavior.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom dotenv import dotenv_values\nimport io\n\n# Test case 1: Basic variable substitution\nenv_content = \"b=c\\na=${b}\"\nstream = io.StringIO(env_content)\nresult = dotenv_values(stream=stream, interpolate=True)\nprint(\"Expected: {'a': 'c', 'b': 'c'}\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result}\")\n\n# Test case 2: Default value substitution\nenv_content2 = \"a=${missing:-default_value}\"\nstream2 = io.StringIO(env_content2)\nresult2 = dotenv_values(stream=stream2, interpolate=True)\nprint(\"Expected: {'a': 'default_value'}\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result2}\")\n\n# Test case 3: Complex interpolation\nenv_content3 = \"b=hello\\na=x${b}y\"\nstream3 = io.StringIO(env_content3)\nresult3 = dotenv_values(stream=stream3, interpolate=True)\nprint(\"Expected: {'a': 'xhelloy', 'b': 'hello'}\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {result3}\")\n```\n\nThe variable substitution is producing incorrect results where variable names and default values appear to be mixed up."
